{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to her: Two nations are in your womb.</b> The opposite of what you thought — but there is one domain. True, two children are in your womb: one will be a worshiper of HaShem and one a worshipper of idolatry, yet HaShem is one and there is none besides Him. And some say that it was stated (Genesis 25:21), ״וַיֶּעְתַּר יִצְחָק לַה׳ לְנֹכַח אִשְׁתּוֹ״, because he was a righteous man the son of a righteous man, therefore it was assured that from his side there would be worthy seed. But he was afraid on his wife's side, for she was the daughter of Bethuel and the sister of Laban — lest some unfit seed emerge from her, seeing that she was barren, and barrenness stems from her. Therefore he was afraid lest unfit seed come forth from her, as Ishmael came forth from Hagar — and perhaps this was the very cause of her barrenness. And when the children struggled within her, one was thrashing to emerge toward the entrance of the house of study and one was thrashing to emerge toward the entrance of idolatry; through this she sensed that surely one would be righteous and one wicked. Therefore she said, ״לָמָּה זֶּה אָנֹכִי״ — for I am like Hagar, and what am I better than she? And why did I pray? ״וַתֵּלֶךְ לִדְרֹשׁ אֶת ה׳״ — what did my prayer avail? And HaShem said to her, ״שְׁנֵי גוֹיִם בְּבִטְנֵךְ״ — this is Rabbi and Antoninus. And her prayer availed in that even from Esau there emerged worthy seed such as Antoninus and other righteous converts, which was not so with Ishmael — and in this you are better than Hagar."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:04.653812302Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}